# Juniper JunOS Firmware Signatures
# Matches JunOS package components and the proprietary 55AA block-compressed format
#
# Install: cp juniper_junos.magic ~/.local/share/radare2/magic/
# Usage:   /m ~/.local/share/radare2/magic/juniper_junos.magic

# =============================================================================
# JunOS 55AA Block-Compressed ISO
# =============================================================================
# Found as overlay appended after the ELF section data in domestic package ELFs.
# The 55AA header sits at overlay_start + 0x198 (after zero padding).
# Structure: 55AA(2) + flags(2) + self_offset(4) + num_blocks(4) + meta(4)
# Followed by TOC of (offset:4, size:4) pairs, then raw deflate blocks.
# Decompresses to an ISO 9660 filesystem containing the full JunOS userland.
#
# See: /aether/vault/ArchSpecs/maps/juniper_junos_domestic_decompress.md
# Tool: /aether/scripts/junos_domestic_decompress.py

0	beshort		0x55aa		Juniper JunOS 55AA block-compressed image
>2	beshort		0x0643		\b, format v1 (deflate blocks)
>8	belong		x		\b, %u blocks
>14	beshort		0x0800		\b, ISO sector-aligned

# =============================================================================
# JunOS Domestic Package ELF (interpreter = /red/herring)
# =============================================================================
# Juniper uses "/red/herring" as the ELF interpreter path for their self-extracting
# package binaries. This is unique to JunOS — no other vendor uses this string.
# The ELF contains both the JunOS monolithic binary AND an appended compressed ISO.
# MIPS64 big-endian, 32-bit mode (ELF32 MSB).

0	belong		0x7f454c46	
>5	byte		0x02		
>16	beshort		0x0002		
>18	beshort		0x0008		
>0x100	search/512	/red/herring	Juniper JunOS domestic package ELF (MIPS, /red/herring interpreter)\b
>>0	byte		x		\b, contains 55AA block-compressed ISO as overlay

# =============================================================================
# JunOS Package Metadata (inside .tgz outer tarball)
# =============================================================================
# The metatags file at the root of the outer tarball identifies package components.

0	string		KERNEL=		Juniper JunOS package metatags
>0	search/128	ROOTFS=		\b, has rootfs

# =============================================================================
# JunOS Package Comment (FreeBSD pkg format)
# =============================================================================
# The +COMMENT file inside the outer tarball contains the version string.

0	string		JUNOS\ Software\ Release	Juniper JunOS package comment
>24	byte		0x5b		\b, version:
>>25	string		x		\b %.40s

# =============================================================================
# JunOS Compressed ISO fstype marker (inside domestic ELF strings)
# =============================================================================
# Embedded string that identifies the compressed ISO format.
# Found via: strings domestic_elf | grep "fstype=iso9660"

0	string		fstype=iso9660,\ compressed,\ packageName=	Juniper JunOS compressed ISO descriptor
>42	string		x	\b, package: %.64s
